!
! The price per unit across offers (fairground_rules.h FR3), in Trebago:
! the sum of the offers' prices over the sum of their units, an exact
! reduced rational, never rounded (7 over 2 units is 7/2). Each price is
! 0 or more and each offer holds at least 1 unit: bad counts the offers
! that do not, and the answer is divided by 1 - min(1, bad), so any one
! of them is a division by zero, refused. A sum past 64 bits is refused by
! Trebago itself, never wrapped.
trebago offer_unit_price
  in  price(n), units(n)
  out unit
  var bad(n)
  bad(i) = min(1, max(0, 0 - price(i))) + min(1, max(0, 1 - units(i)))
  unit = sum(i, price(i)) / sum(i, units(i)) / (1 - min(1, sum(i, bad(i))))
end
